  Source file: ComingSoon-Regular.ttf from https://github.com/google/fonts, apache/comingsoon,
  commit 0fc4c4f4a270a62fa1b769c7289a994cbf199b03,
  sha256 cf81388f587ff6122de1a705d1070b8f00abccdba66108509908b5d10715068c.

Changes (2026-10-14, Bart Slot, for History Portal's speech balloons):

  - Every glyph outline offset outward by 7 units a side (UPM 1000) with a round brush, so stems
    go from about 55 to about 69 units (+25%): a SemiBold (usWeightClass 600).
  - Outlines rendered and retraced (potrace): overlaps removed, contour direction corrected.
  - Units per em changed from 1024 to 1000; vertical metrics scaled to match.
  - Side bearings: the original's, plus 8.5 units a side for the heavier ink.
  - Kerning: the original 861 GPOS pairs, kept and scaled to UPM 1000. The legacy kern table
    and the TrueType hinting are not carried over.
  - "!" and "?" redrawn (version 1.001): the dot is the period's, with ~100 units of white
    above it; the "!" stem tapers to a point, and the "?" tail ends higher, rounded.
  - Renamed to "ComicRoma Balloon".

Build: branding/historyportalBranding/font-build/balloon (make.sh, balloon.py).
